--- OPERATIONAL NOTES -------------------------------------------------------
 * NEW campaign directory (out_c4/...), fresh archive, HV history restarts:
   the objective definition changed, so Campaign-3 values are not comparable.
 * Cost: +~2 min on a ~110 min evaluation (~3%).
 * Noise: per-seed core F_dH sd ~0.007-0.03 at these settings (measured in
   core_rescore); with per-design seeds this is i.i.d. across designs, the
   GP noise term absorbs it, and the end-of-campaign two-stage ranking
   resolves finalists exactly as in Campaign 3 (rank_front_peaking.py needs
   the same one-line switch to the core model for its re-evaluations).
 * The entropy sentinel: if core_entropy_conv > core_inactive appears in the
   archive, that design's peaking carries source-convergence bias; the
   between-block review should list them (one grep of the checkpoint).
 * g_peak at 2.0 now BINDS (best measured design: 2.019 +/- 0.007). Keeping
   2.0 is deliberate: the campaign's question becomes whether ANY corner of
   the five-variable space reaches it. Expect low feasible fractions early.
